var e={missionQuestion:{nb:`Hva forteller kildene om Josefs reise?`,en:`What do the sources say about Joseph’s journey?`},id:`keiserens-befaling`,episode:7,door:7,title:{nb:`Keiserens befaling`,en:`The emperor’s decree`},reference:`Luk 2,1–7`,place:`cesarea`,prologue:[{image:`maps/cesarea-torg.webp`,text:{nb:`Lukas forteller om Josefs og Marias reise. Finn ut hvor de dro, og hvorfor. Etterpå sammenligner du to tekster om når reisen skjedde.`,en:`Luke tells of Joseph and Mary’s journey. Find out where they went, and why. Then compare two texts about when the journey happened.`}},{image:`art/lukas.webp`,text:{nb:`Vi leser Lukas og ser på gamle spor. Hva forteller kildene om innskrivingen?`,en:`We read Luke and look at old clues. What do the sources tell us about the census?`}}],intro:{nb:`Cæsarea, havnebyen der den romerske stattholderen bor.`,en:`Caesarea, the harbour city where the Roman governor lives.`},outro:{nb:`Lukas forteller om reisen til Betlehem. Vi vet ikke sikkert hvordan innskrivingen ble ordnet. Spørsmålet om tidspunktet står åpent.`,en:`Luke tells of the journey to Bethlehem. We do not know exactly how the census was arranged. The question about its date remains open.`},map:[`################..##############`,`################..##############`,`##############....##############`,`#############.......############`,`############........############`,`#########......##.......########`,`##########.....###...###########`,`###########..........###########`,`###########.........############`,`######.#...###...##...##########`,`#####......###...##...##########`,`#####..#######...########.###..#`,`................................`,`..#.#..#.##..#....#..#..#..#.#..`,`########.##..#....#..#..########`,`#######..#############..########`,`#######..##############..#######`,`#######..##############..#######`,`#######..##############..#######`,`################################`,`################################`],background:`cesarea-torg.webp`,mood:`tense`,areas:[{id:`skrivestue`,map:[`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`######.....#########......######`,`######......########......######`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#############......#############`,`#############......#############`,`#############......#############`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`],background:`skrivestue.webp`,scale:2.7,ambience:`street`},{id:`tollboden`,map:[`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`######......########......######`,`######......########......######`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#############......#############`,`#############......#############`,`#############......#############`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`],background:`tollbod.webp`,scale:2.6,ambience:`street`}],start:{x:20,y:9},entities:[{id:`lukas`,kind:`person`,x:18,y:8,name:{nb:`Lukas`,en:`Luke`},look:`luke`,portrait:`lukas.webp`,interactions:[{not:[`oppdrag`],say:[{nb:`Hvor reiste Josef, og hvorfor? Les fortellingen min i skrivestua. Etterpå finner vi ut hvorfor folk fryktet en telling.`,en:`Where did Joseph travel, and why? Read my account in the writing room. Then we find out why people feared a census.`}],set:[`oppdrag`]},{has:[`reisen-lost`,`kornet-veid`,`kvirinius-lost`],not:[`avsluttet`],say:[{nb:`Godt arbeid! Du leste fortellingen, veide skatten og sjekket tidspunktet. Noen spørsmål står åpne.`,en:`Good work! You read the account, weighed the tax and checked the date clues. Some questions stay open.`},{nb:`I morgen følger vi Josef på veien sørover.`,en:`Tomorrow we follow Joseph on the road south.`}],set:[`avsluttet`]},{has:[`avsluttet`],not:[],say:[{nb:`I morgen følger vi Josef på veien sørover.`,en:`Tomorrow we follow Joseph on the road south.`}],set:[]},{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`avsluttet`],say:[{nb:`Når du har nok, kommer jeg med sakene.`,en:`When you have enough, I will bring you the cases.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Tollboden, skrivestua, og folkene på torget. Og les steinene.`,en:`The customs house, the writing room, and the people in the square. And read the stones.`}]}]},{id:`dor-skrivestue`,kind:`place`,x:14,y:2,name:{nb:`Skrivestua`,en:`The writing room`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`skrivestue`,x:15,y:14}},{id:`dor-tollboden`,kind:`place`,x:25,y:11,name:{nb:`Tollboden`,en:`The customs house`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`tollboden`,x:15,y:14}},{id:`soldat`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:soldat`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Soldatens utsagn`,en:`The soldier’s account`},body:[{nb:`Augustus vant borgerkrigene. Han ble hyllet som frelser. Folk knyttet fred, veier, havner og lov til styret hans.`,en:`Augustus won the civil wars. He was hailed as saviour. People linked peace, roads, harbours and law with his rule.`},{nb:`Han forteller selv om tre tellinger av romerske borgere. Det er ikke det samme som innskrivingen Lukas forteller om.`,en:`He records three counts of Roman citizens. Those are not the same as the census Luke tells about.`}]},kind:`person`,x:28,y:13,name:{nb:`Den romerske soldaten`,en:`The Roman soldier`},look:`soldier`,portrait:`soldier.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:soldat`],say:[{nb:`Augustus vant borgerkrigene. Han ble hyllet som frelser. Folk knyttet fred, veier, havner og lov til styret hans.`,en:`Augustus won the civil wars. He was hailed as saviour. People linked peace, roads, harbours and law with his rule.`},{nb:`Han forteller selv om tre tellinger av romerske borgere. Det er ikke det samme som innskrivingen Lukas forteller om.`,en:`He records three counts of Roman citizens. Those are not the same as the census Luke tells about.`}],set:[`spor:soldat`,`spor:pax`,`fakta:augustus`]},{not:[`oppdrag`],say:[{nb:`Snakk med Lukas først.`,en:`Speak with Luke first.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Frelser og fredsbringer. Slik kaller vi Augustus.`,en:`Saviour and bringer of peace. That is what we call Augustus.`}]}]},{id:`kjopmann`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:kjopmann`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Kjøpmannens utsagn`,en:`The merchant’s account`},body:[{nb:`Skatt? Jeg betaler toll i havna og ved byporten. Og så kommer skatten.`,en:`Tax? I pay the toll at the harbour and at the city gate. Then there is the tax.`},{nb:`Hver tollbod har sine menn, og de tar sitt.`,en:`Every customs post has its men, and they take their share.`},{nb:`En telling kan brukes til å regne ut skatt. Derfor kunne folk frykte den. Men det alene viser ikke hva som skjedde.`,en:`A count can be used to work out tax. People could fear it. That alone does not tell us what happened.`}]},kind:`person`,x:20,y:6,name:{nb:`Kjøpmannen`,en:`The merchant`},look:`trader`,portrait:`trader.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:kjopmann`],say:[{nb:`Skatt! En telling brukes til å regne ut skatt, og derfor frykter folk den. Vei kornsekken min i tollboden, så ser du.`,en:`Tax! A census is used to work out tax, so people fear it. Weigh my grain sack in the customs house and see.`}],set:[`spor:kjopmann`,`fakta:skatt`,`kornsekk`]},{has:[`spor:kjopmann`],not:[`kornsekk`],say:[{nb:`Kan du veie kornsekken min? Ta den med til vekta i tollboden.`,en:`Can you weigh my sack of grain? Take it to the scales in the customs house.`}],set:[`kornsekk`]},{has:[`kornet-veid`],say:[{nb:`Kornet er veid, og keiseren har fått sin del. Takk, lærling! Resten kan jeg selge.`,en:`The grain is weighed, and the emperor has had his share. Thank you, apprentice! I can sell the rest.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Toll, toll, toll. Og så skatt.`,en:`Customs, customs, customs. And then tax.`}]}]},{id:`fisker`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:fisker`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Fiskerens utsagn`,en:`The fisherman’s account`},body:[{nb:`Selv fisken teller de. En del av fangsten går til tollerne før jeg får selge resten, og så går prisen opp. Slik er det ved sjøen i Galilea også, sier de, bare at der går det til kongen.`,en:`They even count the fish. Part of the catch goes to the tax men before I can sell the rest, and then the price goes up. By the lake in Galilee too, they say, only there it goes to the king.`}]},kind:`person`,x:8,y:17,name:{nb:`Fiskeren`,en:`The fisherman`},look:`fisher`,portrait:`fisher.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:fisker`],say:[{nb:`Selv fisken teller de. En del av fangsten går til tollerne før jeg får selge resten, og så går prisen opp. Slik er det ved sjøen i Galilea også, sier de, bare at der går det til kongen.`,en:`They even count the fish. Part of the catch goes to the tax men before I can sell the rest, and then the price goes up. By the lake in Galilee too, they say, only there it goes to the king.`}],set:[`spor:fisker`]},{say:[{nb:`Vil du prøve garnet? Fisken står tett.`,en:`Want to try the net? The water is thick with fish.`}],play:{game:`fish`,title:{nb:`Fang fisken`,en:`Catch the fish`},win:`spill-fisk`}}]},{id:`kone`,kind:`person`,x:9,y:9,name:{nb:`Den gamle kona`,en:`The old woman`},look:`oldwoman`,portrait:`oldwoman.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:kone`],say:[{nb:`Jeg husker en telling da Kvirinius styrte Syria for romerne. Folk måtte si hva de eide, og noen gjorde opprør.`,en:`I remember a census when Quirinius ruled Syria for Rome. People had to say what they owned, and some rebelled.`},{nb:`Da var kong Herodes død, og romerne styrte Judea selv.`,en:`By then King Herod was dead, and the Romans ruled Judea themselves.`}],set:[`spor:kone`]},{not:[`oppdrag`],say:[{nb:`Snakk med Lukas først.`,en:`Speak with Luke first.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Kvirinius og tellingen. Det glemmer ingen.`,en:`Quirinius and the census. Nobody forgets that.`}]}],evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:kone`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Gjenfortelling · Josefus 18.1–2`,en:`Retelling · Josephus 18.1–2`},body:[{nb:`Josefus, en jødisk historieskriver som levde like etter Jesus, beskriver en telling under Kvirinius etter kong Herodes’ død. Da gjorde noen opprør.`,en:`Josephus, a Jewish historian who lived just after Jesus, describes a census under Quirinius after King Herod’s death. Some people rebelled then.`}]}},{id:`driver`,kind:`person`,x:12,y:8,name:{nb:`Eseldriveren`,en:`The donkey driver`},look:`driver`,portrait:`driver.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:driver`],say:[{nb:`Jeg kjører varer til Galilea og møter folk på veien. Men jeg kjenner ikke reglene for Josefs reise.`,en:`I carry goods to Galilee and meet people on the road. But I do not know the rules for Joseph’s journey.`},{nb:`På noen mynter står keiserens navn og et år fra styret hans. Det kan hjelpe oss å finne året.`,en:`Some coins show the emperor’s name and a year of his rule. That can help us find the year.`}],set:[`spor:driver`]},{say:[{nb:`Les rullen i skrivestua. Der ser du hva Lukas forteller om reisen.`,en:`Read the scroll in the writing room. It shows what Luke tells about the journey.`}]}],evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:driver`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Eseldriverens utsagn`,en:`The donkey driver’s account`},body:[{nb:`Han frakter varer til Galilea og møter folk på veien. Samtalen gir oss ikke bevarte opplysninger om reglene for Josefs reise.`,en:`He carries goods to Galilee and meets people on the road. His conversation gives us no surviving information about the rules for Joseph’s journey.`}]}},{id:`gutt`,kind:`person`,x:24,y:18,name:{nb:`Gutten på brygga`,en:`The boy on the pier`},look:`boy`,portrait:`boy.webp`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Har du sett sølvmynten i støvet der borte? En gammel en, med keiser Augustus på. Faren hans, Julius, kaller de gud!`,en:`Have you seen the silver coin in the dust over there? An old one, with Emperor Augustus on it. His father, Julius, they call a god!`}],set:[`fakta:mynt`]}]},{id:`kobbermynt`,kind:`thing`,x:13,y:4,name:{nb:`Kobbermynten fra stattholderen`,en:`The governor’s copper coin`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En gammel kobbermynt ligger i støvet ved boden. Slike mynter lot stattholderen i Judea lage. De har keiserens navn og et år fra styret hans. Det kan hjelpe oss å finne året.`,en:`An old copper coin lies in the dust by the stall. The governor of Judea had coins like this made. They show the emperor’s name and a year of his rule. That can help us find the year.`}],set:[`spor:milestein`]}]},{id:`pilatus`,kind:`thing`,x:10,y:5,name:{nb:`Innskriften med Pilatus`,en:`The inscription with Pilate`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`På steinen fra Cæsarea står navnet Pontius Pilatus og tittelen prefekt i Judea. Prefekt var en romersk leder. Noen av bokstavene er ødelagt og fylt inn av forskere.`,en:`The stone from Caesarea names Pontius Pilate as prefect of Judea. A prefect was a Roman official. Some letters are damaged and have been filled in by scholars.`}],set:[`spor:pilatus`,`fakta:pilatus`]}],evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:pilatus`,mark:`kilde`,title:{nb:`Ekte innskrift · Cæsarea · Forenklet forklaring`,en:`Real inscription · Caesarea · Simplified explanation`},body:[{nb:`Steinen navngir Pontius Pilatus som prefekt i Judea. Prefekt var en romersk leder. Noen ødelagte bokstaver er fylt inn av forskere.`,en:`The stone names Pontius Pilate as prefect of Judea. A prefect was a Roman official. Scholars have filled in some damaged letters.`}],symbol:`stone`}},{id:`mynt`,kind:`thing`,x:16,y:10,name:{nb:`Sølvmynten i støvet`,en:`The silver coin in the dust`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En sølvmynt med keiser Augustus. På den står det at han er sønn av en gud. I byen Priene hogde de inn mer om ham i stein: Fødselsdagen hans var godt budskap for verden.`,en:`A silver coin with Emperor Augustus. It says he is the son of a god. In the city of Priene they carved more about him in stone: his birthday was good news for the world.`}],set:[`spor:mynt`]}],evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:mynt`,mark:`kilde`,title:{nb:`Gjenfortelling · Priene-innskriften og Luk 2,10–11`,en:`Retelling · The Priene inscription and Luke 2:10–11`},body:[{nb:`Priene-innskriften: Augustus’ fødselsdag ble kalt starten på godt budskap for verden.`,en:`Priene inscription: Augustus’s birthday was called the beginning of good news for the world.`},{nb:`Lukas: Engelen kom med godt budskap. Jesus, en frelser, var født.`,en:`Luke: the angel brought good news. Jesus, a saviour, had been born.`},{nb:`Ordene står ikke på mynten, men i steinen fra Priene og hos Lukas.`,en:`The words are not written on the coin, but in the stone from Priene and in Luke.`}],symbol:`coin`}},{id:`vei-jerusalem`,kind:`place`,x:31,y:12,name:{nb:`Veien til Jerusalem`,en:`The road to Jerusalem`},look:`hotspot`,travelTo:`jerusalem`},{id:`dor-ut-skrivestue`,kind:`place`,x:15,y:17,name:{nb:`Ut på torget`,en:`Out to the square`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`main`,x:15,y:2},area:`skrivestue`},{id:`tidslinje`,kind:`thing`,x:8,y:7,name:{nb:`Lukas’ liste`,en:`Luke’s list`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Fra Bibelen: Lista er laget fra Luk 3,1–2. Her nevner Lukas flere herskere for å fortelle når Johannes sto fram.`,en:`From the Bible: this list is made from Luke 3:1–2. Luke names several rulers to tell when John began his work.`},{nb:`Tiberius’ femtende år. Pontius Pilatus landshøvding i Judea, Herodes fyrste over Galilea, broren Filip over Iturea, Lysanias over Abilene.`,en:`The fifteenth year of Tiberius. Pontius Pilate governor of Judea, Herod ruler of Galilee, his brother Philip of Ituraea, Lysanias of Abilene.`},{nb:`Annas og Kaifas øversteprester. Sju navn, ett år.`,en:`Annas and Caiaphas high priests. Seven names, one year.`}],set:[`spor:tidslinje`]}],area:`skrivestue`},{id:`edikt`,kind:`thing`,x:18,y:9,artHit:{x:17.8,y:3.6,width:2.3,height:1.9},name:{nb:`Rullen om Josefs reise`,en:`The scroll about Joseph’s journey`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`📜 Gjenfortalt fra Luk 2,1–7. Rullen er ikke en bevart befaling fra keiseren.`,en:`📜 Retold from Luke 2:1–7. The scroll is not a surviving order from the emperor.`},{nb:`Keiser Augustus ba om innskriving: Folk skulle skrives inn i lister. Folk dro hver til sin by. Josef dro til Betlehem, fordi han var i slekt med kong David. Maria var med. Jesus ble født i Betlehem.`,en:`Augustus ordered a census: people’s names were to be listed. People went each to their own town. Joseph went to Bethlehem because he was related to King David. Mary went with him. Jesus was born in Bethlehem.`}],set:[`spor:edikt`,`spor:notat`]}],area:`skrivestue`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:edikt`,mark:`kilde`,title:{nb:`Gjenfortelling · Luk 2,1–7`,en:`Retelling · Luke 2:1–7`},body:[{nb:`Keiser Augustus ba om innskriving: Folk skulle skrives inn i lister. Folk dro hver til sin by. Josef dro til Betlehem, fordi han var i slekt med kong David. Maria var med. Jesus ble født i Betlehem.`,en:`Augustus ordered a census: people’s names were to be listed. People went each to their own town. Joseph went to Bethlehem because he was related to King David. Mary went with him. Jesus was born in Bethlehem.`}],symbol:`scroll`}},{id:`notat`,kind:`thing`,x:15,y:9,artHit:{x:14.5,y:3.8,width:2.7,height:1.7},name:{nb:`Lukas’ notat`,en:`Luke’s note`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Fra Bibelen: Lukas begynner fortellingen i Herodes’ tid (Luk 1,5). Han knytter innskrivingen til Kvirinius, som styrte Syria (2,2).`,en:`From the Bible: Luke begins in Herod’s time (Luke 1:5). He links the census to Quirinius, who governed Syria (2:2).`},{nb:`Vi kjenner en telling under Kvirinius etter Herodes’ død. Hvordan passer tidspunktene sammen? Det er fortsatt et spørsmål.`,en:`We know of a census under Quirinius after Herod’s death. How do the dates fit together? That is still a question.`}],set:[`spor:notat`]}],area:`skrivestue`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:notat`,mark:`kilde`,title:{nb:`Gjenfortelling · Luk 1,5 og 2,1–2`,en:`Retelling · Luke 1:5 and 2:1–2`},body:[{nb:`Lukas begynner fortellingen i Herodes’ tid. Han knytter innskrivingen til Kvirinius, som styrte Syria.`,en:`Luke begins his account in Herod’s time. He links the census to Quirinius, who governed Syria.`}],symbol:`note`}},{id:`dor-ut-tollboden`,kind:`place`,x:15,y:17,name:{nb:`Ut til havna`,en:`Out to the harbour`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`main`,x:25,y:12},area:`tollboden`},{id:`skatteskriver`,kind:`person`,x:20,y:9,name:{nb:`Skatteskriveren`,en:`The tax scribe`},look:`scribe`,portrait:`scribe.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:skatteskriver`],say:[{nb:`En innskriving fører folk på lister. Listene kunne brukes til å regne ut skatt. Reglene var ikke like overalt.`,en:`A census puts people on lists. The lists could be used to work out tax. The rules were not the same everywhere.`},{nb:`Her fører jeg navn og eiendeler på lista mi. Men jeg vet ikke hvilke regler som gjaldt for Josef.`,en:`Here I enter names and possessions on my list. But I do not know which rules applied to Joseph.`},{nb:`Lukas forteller at Josef var av slekten til kong David. Derfor dro han til Betlehem. Maria var med.`,en:`Luke says Joseph came from the family of King David. That is why he went to Bethlehem. Mary went with him.`},{nb:`Kanskje eide familien jord der. Det er et forslag, ikke noe vi vet.`,en:`Perhaps the family owned land there. That is a suggestion, not something we know.`}],set:[`spor:skatteskriver`,`spor:hjemby`,`fakta:manntall`]},{has:[`kornet-veid`],not:[`skriverens-kvittering`],say:[{nb:`Ført i registeret: navn, by, korn. Slik vet keiseren hva han har.`,en:`Entered in the register: name, town, grain. That is how the emperor knows what he has.`}],set:[`skriverens-kvittering`]},{not:[`oppdrag`],say:[{nb:`Snakk med Lukas først.`,en:`Speak with Luke first.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Hvordan innskrivingen foregikk for Josef, vet vi ikke sikkert.`,en:`We do not know exactly how the census worked for Joseph.`}]}],area:`tollboden`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`spor:skatteskriver`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Skatteskriverens utsagn`,en:`The tax scribe’s account`},body:[{nb:`Listene hans er ikke bevarte dokumenter om innskrivingen i Luk 2. En innskriving fører folk på lister, og slike lister kunne brukes til skatt. Reglene var ikke like overalt.`,en:`His lists are not surviving records of the census in Luke 2. A census lists people, and such lists could be used for tax. The rules differed between places.`},{nb:`Lukas forteller at Josef dro til Betlehem fordi han var av Davids slekt. At familien kanskje eide jord der, er et forslag, ikke noe vi vet.`,en:`Luke says Joseph went to Bethlehem because he belonged to David’s family. The idea that his family may have owned land there is a suggestion, not something we know.`}]}},{id:`register`,kind:`thing`,x:17,y:9,name:{nb:`Registeret`,en:`The register`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`🎭 En rull med navn, familier og jordstykker. Vi har ikke Josefs innskrivingsliste.`,en:`🎭 A scroll listing names, families and plots of land. We do not have Joseph’s census record.`}],set:[`spor:register`]}],area:`tollboden`},{id:`vekt`,kind:`thing`,x:14,y:9,name:{nb:`Vekta`,en:`The scales`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{has:[`kornsekk`],not:[`kornet-veid`],say:[{nb:`Sett lodd på vekta til begge sider står like høyt. Den tyngste siden går ned.`,en:`Put weights on the scales until both sides are level. The heavier side goes down.`}],set:[`spor:vekt`],play:{game:`scale`,title:{nb:`Vei kornet`,en:`Weigh the grain`},win:`kornet-veid`,data:{targets:[5,11,19],weights:[1,2,3,4,6,12]},key:!0}},{has:[`kornet-veid`],not:[],say:[{nb:`Kornet er veid! I leken får keiseren 1 av 10 like deler som skatt. Kjøpmannen beholder resten.`,en:`The grain is weighed! In the game, the emperor gets 1 out of 10 equal shares as tax. The merchant keeps the rest.`}],set:[]},{has:[],not:[],say:[{nb:`En stor vekt for korn og olje. Skatten betales ofte i varer, ikke i mynt. Skriveren veier, noterer og tar keiserens del.`,en:`Large scales for grain and oil. Tax is often paid in goods, not coin. The scribe weighs, notes and takes the emperor’s share.`},{nb:`Kjøpmannen på torget har en kornsekk som skal veies.`,en:`The merchant in the square has a sack of grain to be weighed.`}],set:[`spor:vekt`]}],area:`tollboden`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`kornet-veid`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Kornleken`,en:`The grain game`},body:[{nb:`I leken går 1 av 10 like deler av kornet til keiseren som skatt. Kjøpmannen får beholde resten.`,en:`In the game, 1 out of 10 equal shares of grain goes to the emperor as tax. The merchant keeps the rest.`},{nb:`Dette er reglene i leken. De viser ikke hvor mye skatt folk betalte på Josefs reise.`,en:`These are the rules of the game. They do not show how much tax people paid on Joseph’s journey.`}],shares:{caption:{nb:`Ti like deler i kornleken`,en:`Ten equal shares in the grain game`},groups:[{label:{nb:`Keiseren · 1 del`,en:`Emperor · 1 share`},count:1},{label:{nb:`Kjøpmannen · 9 deler`,en:`Merchant · 9 shares`},count:9}]},symbol:`scales`}},{id:`mynt-1`,kind:`thing`,x:3,y:13,name:{nb:`En tollmynt`,en:`A toll coin`},look:`hotspot`,hiddenWhen:`mynt:1`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En kobbermynt. Tollvakten vil ha fire.`,en:`A copper coin. The toll guard wants four.`}],set:[`mynt:1`]}]},{id:`mynt-2`,kind:`thing`,x:7,y:16,name:{nb:`En tollmynt`,en:`A toll coin`},look:`hotspot`,hiddenWhen:`mynt:2`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En kobbermynt. Tollvakten vil ha fire.`,en:`A copper coin. The toll guard wants four.`}],set:[`mynt:2`]}]},{id:`mynt-3`,kind:`thing`,x:22,y:5,name:{nb:`En tollmynt`,en:`A toll coin`},look:`hotspot`,hiddenWhen:`mynt:3`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En kobbermynt. Tollvakten vil ha fire.`,en:`A copper coin. The toll guard wants four.`}],set:[`mynt:3`]}]},{id:`mynt-4`,kind:`thing`,x:16,y:13,name:{nb:`En tollmynt`,en:`A toll coin`},look:`hotspot`,hiddenWhen:`mynt:4`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En kobbermynt. Tollvakten vil ha fire.`,en:`A copper coin. The toll guard wants four.`}],set:[`mynt:4`]}]},{id:`tollvakt`,evidence:{unlockedBy:`toll-betalt`,mark:`dikt`,title:{nb:`Tollvaktens ord`,en:`The toll guard’s words`},body:[{nb:`Fire kobber. Det er tollen. Passér.`,en:`Four coppers. That is the toll. Pass.`}]},kind:`person`,x:26,y:13,name:{nb:`Tollvakten`,en:`The toll guard`},look:`soldier`,portrait:`soldier.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`mynt:1`,`mynt:2`,`mynt:3`,`mynt:4`],not:[`toll-betalt`],say:[{nb:`Fire kobber. Det er tollen. Passér.`,en:`Four coppers. That is the toll. Pass.`}],set:[`toll-betalt`]},{has:[`toll-betalt`],say:[{nb:`Tollen er betalt. Gå inn.`,en:`The toll is paid. Go in.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Toll! Fire kobber for den som vil inn med varer. Har du ikke, så let på torget. Folk mister mynter her hele dagen.`,en:`Toll! Four coppers for anyone going in with goods. If you have none, look around the square. People drop coins here all day.`}]}]},{id:`leke-baat`,kind:`thing`,x:24,y:17,name:{nb:`Båten ved brygga`,en:`The boat by the jetty`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Du ror et lite stykke ut fra brygga og tilbake.`,en:`You row a little way out from the jetty and back.`},{nb:`Tollvakten roper: «Har den båten betalt havneavgift?»`,en:`The customs guard shouts: “Has that boat paid its harbour toll?”`}],fx:`rock`}]},{id:`leke-frukt`,kind:`thing`,x:13,y:3,name:{nb:`Fruktboden`,en:`The fruit stall`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Fikenene ruller inn under bordene. Selgeren sukker: «Først skatten, og så dette.»`,en:`The figs roll under the tables. The seller sighs: “First the tax, and now this.”`}],fx:`tip`}]},{id:`leke-skaal`,kind:`thing`,x:14,y:13,name:{nb:`Bronseskåla`,en:`The bronze bowl`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Klang! En kjøpmann tror stattholderen kommer, og retter seg i ryggen.`,en:`Clang! A merchant thinks the governor is coming and straightens his back.`}],fx:`ring`}]},{id:`leke-palme`,kind:`thing`,x:17,y:2,name:{nb:`Palmen`,en:`The palm tree`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Dadler regner ned. En gutt kommer løpende og samler dem i kappen før du rekker å si noe.`,en:`Dates rain down. A boy comes running and gathers them in his cloak before you can say a word.`}],fx:`shake`}]},{id:`leke-vinde`,kind:`thing`,x:17,y:5,name:{nb:`Brønnvinda`,en:`The well windlass`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Vinda knirker rundt. Bøtta kommer opp full, og en soldat drikker av den før du rekker det.`,en:`The windlass creaks round. The bucket comes up full, and a soldier drinks from it before you can.`}],fx:`spin`}]}],facts:[{id:`augustus`,title:{nb:`Keiserens egen liste`,en:`The emperor’s own list`},body:{nb:`Augustus er keiseren i Lukas’ fortelling om Jesu fødsel (Luk 2,1). Han skrev også om sitt eget styre. I lista hans står tre tellinger av romerske borgere.

Det er Augustus selv som forteller. Lista sier ikke at disse tellingene gjaldt alle som bodde i riket. Den bekrefter derfor ikke alene innskrivingen Lukas forteller om.

Kilde: Augustus, Res Gestae 8.`,en:`Augustus is the emperor in Luke’s account of Jesus’ birth (Luke 2:1). He also wrote about his own rule. His list records three counts of Roman citizens.

Augustus himself is telling us this. The list does not say these counts covered everyone living in the empire. By itself, it therefore does not confirm the census Luke describes.

Source: Augustus, Res Gestae 8.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:augustus`,mark:`kilde`,link:`https://droitromain.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/Anglica/resgest_engl1.htm`},{id:`manntall`,title:{nb:`Gammelt spor: en telling i Egypt`,en:`Old clue: a census in Egypt`},body:{nb:`Et påbud fra Egypt i år 104 ba folk som var borte, om å komme hjem til registrering. Det viser en slik praksis der og da. Det er ikke befalingen Lukas omtaler. Det viser heller ikke at folk i Judea måtte reise til en fjern stamfars by. Kilde: påbudet fra Gaius Vibius Maximus, år 104, bevart på papyrus.`,en:`An order from Egypt in AD 104 told people who were away to return home for registration. It shows that practice there and then. It is not the order Luke describes. It does not show that people in Judea had to travel to a distant ancestor’s town. Source: the edict of Gaius Vibius Maximus, AD 104, preserved on papyrus.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:manntall`,mark:`kilde`,link:`https://droitromain.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/Anglica/Aegypti29_johnson.htm`},{id:`kvirinius`,title:{nb:`Kvirinius og tidspunktet`,en:`Quirinius and the timing`},body:{nb:`Lukas knytter innskrivingen til Kvirinius (Luk 2,2), men begynner fortellingen i Herodes’ dager (1,5). Josefus omtaler en telling under Kvirinius i år 6, etter Herodes’ død (Jødenes historie 18.1). Apg 5,37 omtaler også denne tellingen. Hvordan dette passer sammen, er omdiskutert. En tidligere innskriving og en annen lesning av Luk 2,2 er mulige forslag, ikke funnet dokumentasjon. Vi tar spørsmålet på alvor og har fortsatt tillit til Bibelen. Opplysninger om andre navn avgjør ikke dette spørsmålet alene.`,en:`Luke links the census to Quirinius (Luke 2:2), but begins his account in Herod’s days (1:5). Josephus describes a census under Quirinius in AD 6, after Herod’s death (Antiquities 18.1). Acts 5:37 also mentions this census. How the dates fit together is debated. An earlier census and a different reading of Luke 2:2 are possible suggestions, not discovered records. We take the question seriously and continue to trust the Bible. Information about other names does not settle this question on its own.`},unlockedBy:`kvirinius-lost`,mark:`kilde`,film:`https://vimeo.com/147837526`},{id:`trolig`,title:{nb:`Et spørsmål kan stå åpent`,en:`A question can stay open`},body:{nb:`Vi kan ha gode grunner til tillit og fortsatt ha spørsmål. En gammel kilde kan gi oss navn og steder uten å forklare alle reglene. I denne saken vet vi hva Lukas forteller (Luk 2,1–5). Vi vet ikke sikkert hvordan innskrivingen ble ordnet.`,en:`We can have good reasons for trust and still have questions. An old source can give names and places without explaining every rule. In this case, we know what Luke tells us (Luke 2:1–5). We do not know exactly how the census was arranged.`},unlockedBy:`reisen-lost`,mark:`kilde`},{id:`synkronisme`,title:{nb:`Pilatus i teksten og på steinen`,en:`Pilate in the text and on the stone`},body:{nb:`Fra Bibelen: Luk 3,1–2 nevner keiseren, flere herskere og øversteprestene for å tidfeste Johannes’ virke. Gammelt spor: Pilatus’ navn og tittel er bevart på en stein fra Cæsarea. Et slikt funn støtter en bestemt opplysning. Det avgjør ikke alle andre spørsmål om fortellingen.`,en:`From the Bible: Luke 3:1–2 names the emperor, several rulers and the high priests to date John’s work. Old clue: Pilate’s name and title survive on a stone from Caesarea. Such a find supports one specific piece of information. It does not settle every other question about the account.`},unlockedBy:`datering-lost`,mark:`kilde`,link:`https://bibleproject.com/videos/luke-1-9/`},{id:`pilatus`,title:{nb:`Pilatus-steinen`,en:`The Pilate stone`},body:{nb:`Gammelt spor: Pilatus-steinen ble funnet i Cæsarea i 1961. Innskriften navngir Pontius Pilatus som prefekt i Judea. Den støtter opplysningen om personen og embetet hans. Den avgjør ikke spørsmål om folketellingen eller andre hendelser. Kilde: Pilatus-innskriften; sammenlign Luk 3,1.`,en:`Old clue: the Pilate stone was found at Caesarea in 1961. Its inscription names Pontius Pilate as prefect of Judea. It supports the information about the person and his office. It does not settle questions about the census or other events. Source: the Pilate inscription; compare Luke 3:1.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:pilatus`,mark:`kilde`,discovery:{nb:`En ekte stein fra Cæsarea nevner Pilatus og jobben hans. Den støtter denne opplysningen, men forteller ikke hva som skjedde under folketellingen. Steinen ble funnet i 1961.`,en:`A real stone from Caesarea names Pilate and his office. It supports this detail, but does not tell us what happened during the census. The stone was found in 1961.`}},{id:`skatt`,title:{nb:`Skatt og toll`,en:`Tax and customs`},body:{nb:`Innskrivinger kunne brukes til å regne ut skatt. Apg 5,37 omtaler Judas fra Galilea og opprøret ved tellingen. Det betyr ikke at hver telling alltid økte skatten.`,en:`Censuses could be used to work out tax. Acts 5:37 mentions Judas of Galilee and the revolt at the census. That does not mean every census always raised taxes.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:skatt`,mark:`kilde`},{id:`mynt`,title:{nb:`Keiserens ord`,en:`The emperor’s words`},body:{nb:`Keiseren kunne få titler som frelser. Innskriften fra Priene (9 f.Kr.) omtaler Augustus’ fødselsdag som godt budskap. I Luk 2,10–14 hører gjeterne om et godt budskap, en frelser og fred. Slike ord finnes også i Bibelens profeter, for eksempel Jes 52,7 og 9,5. Om Lukas bevisst setter Jesus opp mot keiseren, er omdiskutert.`,en:`The emperor could receive titles such as saviour. The Priene inscription (9 BC) calls Augustus’ birthday good news. In Luke 2:10–14 the shepherds hear of good news, a saviour and peace. Such words also occur in the biblical prophets, for example Isaiah 52:7 and 9:6. Whether Luke deliberately contrasts Jesus with the emperor is debated.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:mynt`,mark:`kilde`},{id:`diktet`,title:{nb:`Hva er diktet i dag?`,en:`What is made up today?`},unlockedBy:`oppdrag`,mark:`dikt`,body:{nb:`🎭 Diktet i dag: folkene på torget, tollvakten og skatteskriveren, samtalene, kornsekken, skattesatsen, registeret og rullene i skrivestua. 📜 Fra gamle kilder: innskrivingen (Luk 2,1–7), Josefus om Kvirinius, Pilatus-steinen og innskriften fra Priene. Ingen befaling fra Augustus om denne innskrivingen er funnet.`,en:`🎭 Made up today: the people in the square, the toll guard and the tax scribe, the conversations, the grain sack, the tax rate, the register and the scrolls in the writing room. 📜 From old sources: the census (Luke 2:1–7), Josephus on Quirinius, the Pilate stone and the Priene inscription. No order from Augustus about this census has been found.`}}],words:[{id:`pilatus`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`Pilatus`,en:`Pilate`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:pilatus`},{id:`kvirinius`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`Kvirinius`,en:`Quirinius`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:kone`},{id:`augustus`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`Augustus`,en:`Augustus`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:edikt`},{id:`keiser-augustus`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`keiser Augustus`,en:`Emperor Augustus`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:mynt`},{id:`herodes`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`Herodes`,en:`Herod`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:kone`},{id:`david`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`David`,en:`David`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:edikt`},{id:`eseldriveren`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`eseldriveren`,en:`the donkey driver`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:driver`},{id:`fiskeren`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`fiskeren`,en:`the fisherman`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:fisker`},{id:`kjopmannen`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`kjøpmannen`,en:`the merchant`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:kjopmann`},{id:`den-romerske-soldaten`,kind:`person`,form:`m`,text:{nb:`den romerske soldaten`,en:`the Roman soldier`},unlockedBy:`spor:soldat`},{id:`den-gamle-kona`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`den gamle kona`,en:`the old woman`},form:`f`,unlockedBy:`spor:kone`},{id:`fred`,kind:`ting`,text:{nb:`fred`,en:`peace`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:soldat`},{id:`lov`,kind:`ting`,text:{nb:`lov`,en:`law`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:soldat`},{id:`skatt`,kind:`ting`,text:{nb:`skatt`,en:`tax`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:kjopmann`},{id:`skatten`,kind:`ting`,text:{nb:`skatten`,en:`the tax`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`kornet-veid`},{id:`tollen`,kind:`ting`,text:{nb:`tollen`,en:`the toll`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`toll-betalt`},{id:`prisen`,kind:`ting`,form:`m`,text:{nb:`prisen`,en:`the price`},unlockedBy:`spor:fisker`},{id:`i-havna`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`i havna`,en:`at the harbour`},unlockedBy:`spor:kjopmann`},{id:`ved-byporten`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`ved byporten`,en:`at the city gate`},unlockedBy:`spor:kjopmann`},{id:`hver-til-sin-by`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`hver til sin by`,en:`each to their own town`},unlockedBy:`spor:edikt`},{id:`til-betlehem`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`til Betlehem`,en:`to Bethlehem`},unlockedBy:`spor:edikt`},{id:`i-betlehem`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`i Betlehem`,en:`in Bethlehem`},unlockedBy:`spor:edikt`},{id:`i-galilea`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`i Galilea`,en:`in Galilee`},unlockedBy:`spor:fisker`},{id:`til-galilea`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`til Galilea`,en:`to Galilee`},unlockedBy:`spor:driver`},{id:`paa-veien`,kind:`sted`,text:{nb:`på veien`,en:`on the road`},unlockedBy:`spor:driver`},{id:`skatteskriveren`,kind:`person`,text:{nb:`skatteskriveren`,en:`the tax scribe`},form:`m`,unlockedBy:`spor:skatteskriver`},{id:`reise-galilea`,text:{nb:`til Galilea`,en:`to Galilee`},kind:`sted`,answerOnly:!0},{id:`reise-herodes`,text:{nb:`Herodes`,en:`Herod`},kind:`person`,answerOnly:!0,form:`m`},{id:`tid-apent`,text:{nb:`Vi må undersøke hvordan tidspunktene passer sammen`,en:`We need to investigate how the dates fit together`},kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0},{id:`tid-avgjort`,text:{nb:`Lukas og kona nevner samme år`,en:`Luke and the old woman name the same year`},kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0},{id:`pilatus-leder`,kind:`metode`,form:`m`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Pilatus var romersk leder i Judea`,en:`Pilate was a Roman official in Judea`}},{id:`pilatus-fodselsdato`,kind:`metode`,form:`m`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Steinen forteller når Jesus ble født`,en:`The stone tells us when Jesus was born`}},{id:`begge-godt-budskap`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Begge tekstene bruker ordene «godt budskap»`,en:`Both texts use the words “good news”`}},{id:`bare-lukas-budskap`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Bare teksten om Jesus bruker ordene «godt budskap»`,en:`Only the text about Jesus uses the words “good news”`}},{id:`korn-del-skatt`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Keiseren får en del som skatt. Kjøpmannen beholder resten`,en:`The emperor gets a share as tax. The merchant keeps the rest`}},{id:`korn-alt-keiseren`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Tollvakten får en del som toll. Kjøpmannen beholder resten`,en:`The toll guard gets a share as toll. The merchant keeps the rest`}},{id:`augustus-ordre`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Augustus ber om innskriving`,en:`Augustus orders a census`}},{id:`josef-maria-reise`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Josef og Maria reiser til Betlehem`,en:`Joseph and Mary travel to Bethlehem`}},{id:`jesus-fodt`,kind:`metode`,answerOnly:!0,text:{nb:`Jesus blir født i Betlehem`,en:`Jesus is born in Bethlehem`}}],deductions:[{id:`datering`,detective:!0,question:{nb:`Hva forteller steinen om Pilatus?`,en:`What does the stone tell us about Pilate?`},report:[{text:{nb:`{1}.`,en:`{1}.`},gaps:[{choices:[`pilatus-leder`,`pilatus-fodselsdato`]}],hint:{nb:`Se etter mannens navn og jobben hans på kildekortet.`,en:`Look for the man’s name and his job on the source card.`}}],checks:[],done:{nb:`Du knyttet en opplysning til sporet som støtter den. Vi må undersøke andre spørsmål for seg.`,en:`You linked a claim to the clue that supports it. Other questions need their own investigation.`},set:[`datering-lost`],presentation:`statements`,requires:[`spor:pilatus`],sources:[`spor:pilatus`],assessment:{stamp:`troverdig`,claim:{nb:`Pilatus var romersk prefekt i Judea.`,en:`Pilate was the Roman prefect of Judea.`},reason:{nb:`En innskrift fra hans egen tid navngir ham og jobben hans. Derfor har denne opplysningen god historisk støtte. Steinen sier ikke når Jesus ble født.`,en:`An inscription from his own time names him and his office. This gives the claim strong historical support. The stone does not say when Jesus was born.`},reference:{nb:`Kilde: Pilatus-innskriften fra Cæsarea (AE 1963, 104).`,en:`Source: the Pilate inscription from Caesarea (AE 1963, 104).`}}},{id:`reisen`,question:{nb:`Hva forteller Lukas om Josefs reise?`,en:`What does Luke tell us about Joseph’s journey?`},report:[{text:{nb:`Josef dro {1}, etter det Lukas skriver.`,en:`Joseph went {1}, according to Luke’s account.`},gaps:[{choices:[`til-betlehem`,`reise-galilea`]}],hint:{nb:`Les kildekortet her i boka. Hvilken by reiste Josef til?`,en:`Read the source card here in the notebook. Which town did Joseph travel to?`}},{text:{nb:`Josef hørte til familien til kong {1}.`,en:`King {1} was in Joseph’s family long ago.`},gaps:[{choices:[`david`,`reise-herodes`]}],hint:{nb:`Kildekortet her i boka sier hvilken konge Josef var i slekt med.`,en:`The source card here in the notebook names the king in Joseph’s family.`}}],checks:[],done:{nb:`Ja, der står det! Lukas forteller om reisen og Davids slekt. Vi vet ikke sikkert hvordan innskrivingen ble ordnet.`,en:`Yes, there it is! Luke tells of the journey and David’s family. We do not know exactly how the registration was arranged.`},set:[`reisen-lost`],kind:`metode`,requires:[`oppdrag`,`spor:edikt`],sources:[`spor:edikt`]},{id:`kvirinius`,question:{nb:`Hva må vi undersøke mer?`,en:`What do we need to investigate further?`},report:[{text:{nb:`{1}.`,en:`{1}.`},gaps:[{choices:[`tid-apent`,`tid-avgjort`]}],hint:{nb:`Det ene kortet nevner Herodes. Det andre forteller om tiden etterpå. Har vi en sikker dato ennå?`,en:`One card mentions Herod. The other describes a later time. Do we have an exact date yet?`}}],checks:[`flere`,`tidlig`],open:{nb:`Vi kjenner en telling under Kvirinius i år 6. Hvordan den passer med fødselen i Herodes’ tid, er fortsatt et spørsmål.`,en:`We know of a census under Quirinius in AD 6. How it fits the birth in Herod’s time is still a question.`},done:{nb:`Klokt sagt! Her mangler vi brikker om tidspunktet, men vi tar spørsmålet på alvor.`,en:`Wisely said! Pieces are missing here about the date, but we take the question seriously.`},set:[`kvirinius-lost`],assessment:{stamp:`omstridt`,claim:{nb:`Spørsmålet gjelder tidspunktet for innskrivingen.`,en:`The question concerns the date of the registration.`},reason:{nb:`Lukas knytter fortellingen til Herodes og Kvirinius. Josefus beskriver en senere telling. Hvordan opplysningene passer sammen, er ikke avgjort her. Det betyr ikke at hele fortellingen er usann.`,en:`Luke links the account to Herod and Quirinius. Josephus describes a later census. How the details fit together is not settled here. That does not mean the whole account is untrue.`},reference:{nb:`Kilder: Luk 1,5 og 2,1–2; Josefus, Jødenes historie 18.1–2.`,en:`Sources: Luke 1:5 and 2:1–2; Josephus, Antiquities 18.1–2.`}},requires:[`oppdrag`,`spor:kone`,`spor:notat`],sources:[`spor:notat`,`spor:kone`],presentation:`statements`},{id:`keiseren`,detective:!0,question:{nb:`Hva er likt i de to tekstene?`,en:`What is alike in the two texts?`},report:[{text:{nb:`{1}.`,en:`{1}.`},gaps:[{choices:[`begge-godt-budskap`,`bare-lukas-budskap`]}],hint:{nb:`Les én tekst om gangen. Finn ordene «godt budskap» i begge.`,en:`Read one text at a time. Find the words “good news” in both.`}}],checks:[],done:{nb:`Du fant like ord i to ulike tekster. Det er et spor å undersøke. Det viser ikke alene at Lukas brukte den andre teksten.`,en:`You found similar words in two different texts. That is a clue to explore. It does not by itself show that Luke used the other text.`},set:[`keiseren-lost`],kind:`metode`,presentation:`statements`,requires:[`oppdrag`,`spor:mynt`],sources:[`spor:mynt`]},{id:`skatten`,question:{nb:`Hvem får kornet i leken?`,en:`Who gets the grain in the game?`},report:[{text:{nb:`{1}.`,en:`{1}.`},gaps:[{choices:[`korn-del-skatt`,`korn-alt-keiseren`]}],hint:{nb:`Les kortet: Hvem får én del, og hvem beholder resten?`,en:`Read the card: who gets one share, and who keeps the rest?`}}],checks:[],done:{nb:`Du skilte mellom delen til keiseren og resten til kjøpmannen. Skattesatsen er bare en regel i leken.`,en:`You told the emperor’s share apart from the merchant’s share. The tax rate is just a rule of the game.`},set:[`skatten-lost`],kind:`metode`,presentation:`statements`,requires:[`oppdrag`,`kornet-veid`],sources:[`kornet-veid`]},{id:`befalingen`,question:{nb:`Legg tre hendelser fra Lukas’ fortelling i rekkefølge.`,en:`Put three events from Luke’s account in order.`},report:[{id:`ordre-reise-fodsel`,sequence:!0,text:{nb:`Først: {1}. Så: {2}. Til slutt: {3}.`,en:`First: {1}. Next: {2}. Finally: {3}.`},gaps:[{choices:[`augustus-ordre`,`josef-maria-reise`,`jesus-fodt`]},{choices:[`josef-maria-reise`,`augustus-ordre`,`jesus-fodt`]},{choices:[`jesus-fodt`,`augustus-ordre`,`josef-maria-reise`]}],hint:{nb:`Finn befalingen, reisen og fødselen på kortet. Hva skjer først?`,en:`Find the order, the journey and the birth on the card. What happens first?`},feedback:{nb:`Finn befalingen, reisen og fødselen på kortet. Hva skjer først?`,en:`Find the order, the journey and the birth on the card. What happens first?`}}],checks:[],done:{nb:`Slik forteller Lukas om reisen og fødselen (Luk 2,1–7). Vi har ingen bevart befaling fra Augustus om denne innskrivingen.`,en:`This is Luke’s account of the journey and birth (Luke 2:1–7). We have no surviving order from Augustus for this census.`},set:[`befalingen-lost`],kind:`metode`,requires:[`oppdrag`,`spor:edikt`],sources:[`spor:edikt`]}],objectives:[{text:{nb:`Snakk med Lukas`,en:`Talk to Luke`},doneBy:[`oppdrag`]},{text:{nb:`Les om Josefs reise i skrivestua`,en:`Read about Joseph’s journey in the writing room`},doneBy:[`spor:edikt`]},{text:{nb:`Finn reisemålet og familien i teksten`,en:`Find the destination and family in the text`},doneBy:[`reisen-lost`]},{text:{nb:`Vei kjøpmannens korn i tollboden`,en:`Weigh the merchant’s grain in the customs house`},doneBy:[`kornet-veid`]},{text:{nb:`Snakk med den gamle kona på torget`,en:`Talk to the old woman in the square`},doneBy:[`spor:kone`]},{text:{nb:`Finn spørsmålet som står åpent`,en:`Find the question that remains open`},doneBy:[`kvirinius-lost`]},{text:{nb:`Gå tilbake til Lukas`,en:`Return to Luke`},doneBy:[`avsluttet`]}],rewards:[{flag:`datering-lost`,points:20,label:{nb:`Knytt Pilatus til sporet`,en:`Link Pilate to the evidence`},side:!0},{flag:`reisen-lost`,points:10,label:{nb:`Forstå reisen til Betlehem`,en:`Understand the journey to Bethlehem`}},{flag:`kvirinius-lost`,points:20,label:{nb:`Si ærlig fra om det som er uavklart`,en:`Say the open question openly`}},{flag:`keiseren-lost`,points:15,label:{nb:`Hør keiserens ord`,en:`Hear the emperor’s words`},side:!0},{flag:`skatten-lost`,points:10,label:{nb:`Forstå skatten`,en:`Understand the tax`},side:!0},{flag:`befalingen-lost`,points:10,label:{nb:`Sett Lukas’ fortelling i rekkefølge`,en:`Put Luke’s account in order`},side:!0},{flag:`avsluttet`,points:10,label:{nb:`Fullfør dagen med Lukas`,en:`Finish the day with Luke`}},{flag:`spill-fisk`,points:10,label:{nb:`Fang fisken`,en:`Catch the fish`},side:!0},{flag:`spor:register`,points:5,label:{nb:`Les registeret`,en:`Read the register`},side:!0},{flag:`fakta:pilatus`,points:5,label:{nb:`Finn Pilatus i stein`,en:`Find Pilate in stone`},side:!0},{flag:`mynt:1`,points:2,label:{nb:`Finn en kobbermynt`,en:`Find a copper coin`},side:!0},{flag:`mynt:2`,points:2,label:{nb:`Finn en kobbermynt`,en:`Find a copper coin`},side:!0},{flag:`mynt:3`,points:2,label:{nb:`Finn en kobbermynt`,en:`Find a copper coin`},side:!0},{flag:`mynt:4`,points:2,label:{nb:`Finn en kobbermynt`,en:`Find a copper coin`},side:!0},{flag:`toll-betalt`,points:12,label:{nb:`Finn fire kobbermynter og betal tollvakten`,en:`Find four copper coins and pay the toll guard`},side:!0},{flag:`skriverens-kvittering`,points:10,label:{nb:`Hent kvitteringen hos skatteskriveren etter veiingen`,en:`Collect the receipt from the tax scribe after the weighing`},side:!0},{flag:`kornet-veid`,points:10,label:{nb:`Vei kjøpmannens korn`,en:`Weigh the merchant’s grain`},side:!1,activity:!0}],inventory:[{icon:`🪙`,label:{nb:`Kobbermynter`,en:`Copper coins`},flags:[`mynt:1`,`mynt:2`,`mynt:3`,`mynt:4`],goneWhen:`toll-betalt`},{icon:`🌾`,label:{nb:`Kornsekk`,en:`Grain sack`},flags:[`kornsekk`],goneWhen:`kornet-veid`}],ambience:[{sound:`sea`,x:8,y:16,radius:8},{sound:`sea`,x:16,y:16,radius:8},{sound:`sea`,x:23,y:16,radius:8},{sound:`market`,x:12,y:4,radius:5},{sound:`market`,x:21,y:6,radius:5},{sound:`market`,x:15,y:8,radius:4}],claim:{label:{nb:`innskrivingen under Kvirinius`,en:`the registration under Quirinius`},text:{nb:`Innskrivingen da Kvirinius styrte Syria, skjedde mens Herodes ennå var konge (Luk 1,5; 2,1–2).`,en:`The registration when Quirinius governed Syria took place while Herod was still king (Luke 1:5; 2:1–2).`},stamp:`omstridt`,reason:{nb:`Lukas er nøyaktig mange steder. Men Josefus forteller om en telling under Kvirinius omtrent ti år etter at Herodes døde. Forskerne har flere forslag, men saken er ikke avgjort.`,en:`Luke is accurate in many places. But Josephus tells of a count under Quirinius about ten years after Herod died. Scholars have several suggestions, but the matter is not settled.`},traces:[{icon:`✍️`,name:{nb:`Josefus`,en:`Josephus`}},{icon:`🪨`,name:{nb:`Steinen fra Venezia`,en:`The stone in Venice`}},{icon:`🪨`,name:{nb:`Steinen fra Tivoli`,en:`The stone from Tivoli`}}],sources:{nb:`Josefus, *Ant.* 17,355; 18,1–2; 18,26 (W 17.13.5; 18.1.1; 18.2.1): Kvirinius ble sendt «to take account of people’s effects in Syria», og tellingen ble avsluttet «in the thirty-seventh year of Caesar’s victory over Antony at Actium», altså i år 6 e.Kr. Herodes døde i 4 f.Kr., og fordi det ikke finnes noe år 0, er det 9–10 år imellom. Lapis Venetus (CIL III 6687): en telling i Apameia på Kvirinius’ befaling. Lapis Tiburtinus (CIL XIV 3613 = ILS 918, Tivoli 1764): en navnløs stattholder som var legat «for annen gang», kanskje i Syria (Syme). Kokkinos (2012) nevner Kvirinius, Piso og Sentius Saturninus. *Res Gestae* 8 gjelder tellinger av romerske borgere, ikke provinsene. Den viser bare at Augustus telte.`,en:`Josephus, *Ant.* 17.355; 18.1–2; 18.26 (W 17.13.5; 18.1.1; 18.2.1): Quirinius was sent “to take account of people’s effects in Syria”, and the count was finished “in the thirty-seventh year of Caesar’s victory over Antony at Actium”, that is, in AD 6. Herod died in 4 BC, and as there is no year 0, that is 9–10 years apart. Lapis Venetus (CIL III 6687): a census in Apamea on Quirinius’ orders. Lapis Tiburtinus (CIL XIV 3613 = ILS 918, Tivoli 1764): an unnamed governor who was legate “for the second time”, perhaps in Syria (Syme). Kokkinos (2012) names Quirinius, Piso and Sentius Saturninus. *Res Gestae* 8 is about counts of Roman citizens, not of the provinces. It shows only that Augustus counted.`},note:{nb:`At Augustus var keiser, er Troverdig.`,en:`That Augustus was emperor is Trustworthy.`}},goal:[`avsluttet`],solution:`lukas.dor-skrivestue.edikt.reisen.dor-ut-skrivestue.kjopmann.dor-tollboden.vekt.dor-ut-tollboden.kone.kvirinius.lukas.soldat.driver.fisker.fisker.kobbermynt.pilatus.datering.mynt.keiseren.gutt.mynt-1.mynt-2.mynt-3.mynt-4.tollvakt.dor-tollboden.skatteskriver.register.vekt.skatten.skatteskriver.dor-ut-tollboden.dor-skrivestue.tidslinje.notat.befalingen.dor-ut-skrivestue`.split(`.`)};export{e as default};